Let's calculate the value of x_4:
\begin{align*}
x_4 &= (\sqrt[3]{3})^{\sqrt[3]{3}} \\
&= 3^{\sqrt[3]{3}}
\end{align*}
Since 3^1 = 3, we can simplify the expression:
\begin{align*}
x_4 &= 3^{\sqrt[3]{3}} \\
&= 3^1 \\
&= 3
\end{align*}
Therefore, the value of x is 3.
